  "notes": "CONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- Negative: {免|まぬが}れない\n- Te-form: {免|まぬが}れて\n- Past: {免|まぬが}れた\n- Potential: {免|まぬが}れられる\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. Takes を for the thing being avoided.\n\nREADING VARIANT:\nAlso read as {免|まぬか}れる (まぬかれる). Both readings are standard.\n\nUSAGE:\nA relatively formal word, commonly found in news reports and written Japanese. The pattern 〜を{免|まぬが}れない means \"cannot avoid\" or \"is inevitable.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {危険|きけん}を{免|まぬが}れる: to escape danger\n- {責任|せきにん}を{免|まぬが}れる: to be exempt from responsibility\n- {罰|ばつ}を{免|まぬが}れる: to escape punishment\n- {批判|ひはん}を{免|まぬが}れない: to be unable to avoid criticism",
